## 2. Operational checklist (applied to every new visual asset)

1. **Prompt baseline (AAR-12):** scene described concretely; identity-conditioned
   on an approved anchor crop (face + hair, above shoulders — no garment
   inheritance) whenever the Aarohi persona appears. Identity lock + marker lock
   (bindi, open hair) verbatim from Persona Bible §1.
2. **Negative constraints — mandatory block, verbatim in every prompt:**
   "Strictly exclude: any text, letters, numbers, words, captions, subtitles,
   signage, labels, typography of any kind; logos, brand marks, watermarks,
   stamps; user-interface elements, app frames, phone screen UI, fake quotes or
   speech bubbles; irrelevant decorative elements (random patterns, clutter,
   glitch artifacts). The image contains zero written characters."
   Plus surface exclusions when the scene implies boards/screens (cafés, desks,
   shops): "no chalkboards, menu boards, posters, signs, labelled products."
3. **Default deliverable: clean, text-free image.** No embedded copy — story,
   CTA, disclosure and hashtags live in the caption / native reel text layer
   (AAR-12 close-out; supersedes burned-in badge convention for new assets).
4. **Approved-text exception:** only with explicit approval. Deliver BOTH the
   approved-text asset AND a clean no-text variant of the same scene. Prompt
   pins the exact string ("spell it exactly, letter for letter"), the style,
   placement, and excludes every other text source.
5. **Final QC pass before handoff (all gates):** anatomy (hands/fingers),
   identity consistency vs anchor, lighting, skin/texture realism, artifacts,
   scene relevance to the brief, output resolution/aspect vs format spec, and a
   zero-text check across every region (surfaces, cup, walls, clothing).
6. **Document per asset:** model id, output resolution, anchor crop id + SHA-256,
   final asset SHA-256, prompt/exclusion blocks, QC verdict.
7. **Rejection loop:** any failed gate → regenerate with the named fix, re-run
   the FULL QC pass, log rule/finding/remedy/verdict. Never hand off a known
   violation.

